<!--
A todo app with nothing todo-specific in it. Run it through the one binary:

    beet --main=examples/ui/dynamic_view.bsx

Nothing here knows what a todo is. `dynamic_view/schema.json` is a schema
document holding the row schema (`TodoItem`), `dynamic_view/todos.json` is the
data document holding the rows and composing that schema by reference, and every
widget on the page is generated from whichever one it is bound to:

- `<DynamicView/>` reads the list as a table, one column per field of the row.
- `<DynamicForm/>` edits the same list: a control per field per row, a remove
  button beside each row and an add button that appends the row schema's zero.
- `<ToggleSchemaEditor/>` is edit mode, closed by default. Open it and the form
  inside edits the *schema* document, generated from the schema of schemas, and
  Apply commits the new schema and backfills every existing row in one
  transaction (or refuses and touches neither document).

So the demonstration is the loop: open edit mode, add a field named
`is_really_difficult`, choose `Bool` for its schema, press Apply, close edit mode
— and the table has a new column and the form a new control, because both are
generated from the schema that just changed. A commit must leave the rows that
already exist valid, so a *required* field also needs an `on_missing` of
`Default`; leaving the new field optional is the other way to say the same
thing, and a commit with neither is refused in the error line under the form.

Naming which document is which is the whole wiring. `<DocumentBlob>` is a
document that lives in the store (here the entry's own directory), so the schema
document is a sibling declaration the editor points at with `{DocRef($schema)}`
and the data document is the subtree everything else sits in. The widgets name
no schema at all: a document is the authority on the shape of its own value, so
they read it from the document they bind, whenever it arrives.

The two JSON files are the *living* state, not the authored original: editing in
the app rewrites them, so `git diff examples/ui/dynamic_view` is the record of
what the session changed and `git checkout` is the reset.
-->
<CallOnReady {(TuiServer, SweepDescendants)}>
	<CrateCheck features={["tui_server", "json", "fs"]}/>
	<Router>
		<Route path="/" {FixedPage}>
			<DocumentBlob bx:ref="schema" path="dynamic_view/schema.json"/>
			<DocumentBlob path="dynamic_view/todos.json">
				<h1>Todos</h1>
				<DynamicView/>
				<DynamicForm/>
				<ToggleSchemaEditor {DocRef($schema)}/>
			</DocumentBlob>
		</Route>
	</Router>
</CallOnReady>
